{"repositoryId":426150546,"availability":"available","full":"magnesiumlabs/magnesium","name":"magnesium","description":"Sass toolkit for managing design tokens as CSS custom properties.","category":"Design","language":"SCSS","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2021-11-09T08:36:11Z","updated":"2026-09-14T21:31:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://magnesium.dev","topics":["design-system","framework","sass","theme"],"demo":"https://stackblitz.com/~/github.com/magnesiumlabs/magnesium","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.403Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.403Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.403Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.403Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sass toolkit for managing design tokens as CSS custom properties. The model is define → emit → consume: declare tokens as plain Sass maps, emit them as scoped, prefixed custom properties, then reference them in your rules.","This README is a quick overview, the full guides and API reference live at magnesium.dev.","Writing --button-text-color: darkcyan by hand works right up until the token set grows. Magnesium adds three things on top of it:"],"features":["A typo becomes a build error. theme() checks every token against a reference schema, so a misspelled key stops","One source of truth. The same Sass map produces the declarations, the var() references and their fallbacks, so","One prefix to change. Every custom property is namespaced through $prefix, so renaming it is a single line"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/magnesiumlabs/magnesium/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2dae8071c5dec78739cad46cb6ce96c2667c8ef5e25786584829b9e5b454d9d1","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.529Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:46.529Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Sass toolkit for managing design tokens as CSS custom properties. The model is define → emit → con